-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",369,{
[11777]="70068367\n1\tCollect bags of tar sand ([see journal]/3)\tMake your way to the worm habitat in the north-west crags. Search there for patches of black sand and collect three bags for Abido at the expedition encampment.\n2\tYou searched the area and found three full bags of tar sand. Return the filled sacks to Abido at the hunter's expedition in the south-east of the Cape of Umbar.\t\n",
[11778]="700173B0\n1\tTalk to Raf at Anazârmekhem\tRaf is at Anazârmekhem. Pálmar seemed a bit worried about the leader of the Orcs within the Forges and advised that you speak with Raf before you enter the Forges.\n",
[11779]="700173AF\n1\tDefeat Kranklûk\tKranklûk is in the Forges of Khazad-dûm, south-west of Anazârmekhem. Raf has asked you to find and defeat the Black Uruk Kranklûk. He told you to shield yourself from fire and shadow when facing this terrible foe as he fears that it may be something more than a common Uruk.\n2\tTalk to Raf at Anazârmekhem\tRaf is at Anazârmekhem, north-east of the Forges of Khazad-dûm. Kranklûk proved to be a powerful Uruk and perhaps something more. Still, after scaling down the terrible pit that the Forges of Khazad-dûm has become, you found and defeated the foe.\n",
[11780]="70002C8F\n1\tSpeak with Aggy Digweed\tAggy Digweed is at the entrance to the Trestlespan at the northern edge of Trestlebridge. You should speak with Aggy Digweed.\n2\tFind the black-fire at the first encampment\030Find the black-fire at the second encampment\030Find the black-fire at the third encampment\tOrc encampments have been spotted north-east of Trestlebridge. You should investigate the Orc-camps for signs of the black-fire, and carefully destroy any that you find.\n3\tReturn to Aggy Digweed\tAggy Digweed can be found in Trestlebridge. You should return to Aggy Digweed with the news that you destroyed all the remaining crates of incendiary powder that you could find.\n4\tReturn to Captain Trotter\tCaptain Trotter is in Trestlebridge. You should speak with Captain Trotter.\n",
[11781]="70000030\n1\tDefeat brigands at Blackwolds' Roost (total: 6)\tBlackwolds' Roost lies among the ruins south of the Hunter's Lodge. Jon Brackenbrook has asked you to provide a distraction by engaging the brigands at their encampment, Blackwolds' Roost.\n2\tTalk to Jon Brackenbrook\tJon Brackenbrook can be found in the Hunter's Lodge, east of Archet, north of Blackwolds' Roost. You engaged the Blackwolds as Jon Brackenbrook requested, but only time will tell if your efforts were enough. You should return to Jon with your report.\n",
[11782]="700573F6\n1\tComplete deeds in Eriador to earn Honour\tYou have joined Elladan's faction in 'The Tournament of the Twins' and may now do battle with Elrohir's faction members! - Complete deeds in Eriador to earn Honour. - You may be harassed and hunted by member's of Elrohir's faction!\n",
[11783]="700573F8\n1\tYou have joined Elrohir's faction in 'The Tournament of the Twins' and may now do battle with Elladan's faction members! - Complete deeds in Eriador to earn Honour. - You may be harassed and hunted by member's of Elladan's faction!\t\n",
[11784]="70009673\n1\tTalk to Aragorn in Rivendell and travel to the forges\tAragorn is in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. The Elf-smiths of Imladris will reforge the blade that was broken, and Aragorn is waiting to walk with you to the forges where it will be done.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn in Rivendell\tAragorn is in one of the guest rooms along the road that winds up the southern slope of the Vale of Imladris. Andúril, Flame of the West, has been forged from the shards of Narsil, and Aragorn is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[11785]="700717A2\n1\tInspect Amûma's roots (total: 5)\tIrsinith has asked that you inspect Amûma and see how the blight is rotting her roots.\n2\tReturn to Irsinith\tAfter inspecting the roots of Amûma, you discover the severe signs of blight that Irsinith spoke of corrupting the tree.\n",
[11786]="70028FB2\n1\tHelp Wunne make spears more quickly\030Help Rhianu find missing nails and pins for the siege-engines\030Help Gethin deliver the heavy boxes and crates to the other worksites\tThe workers who have slowed the day's progress can be found at the fourth post in Galtrev. The Overseer has demanded that you beat the slow labourers, but there is probably a better way to move things along. You should assist the workers who need help meeting the demands of the White Hand.\n2\tTalk to Flint Ironheart at the fourth worksite\tThe Half-orc overseer, Flint Ironheart, can be found at the fourth worksite in Galtrev. You should speak with the Overseer of this work-camp and show him that the supplies are once again moving along adequately.\n3\tTalk to Gethin in Galtrev\tGethin can be found at the fourth worksite. You should speak with Gethin now that the Overseer is somewhat appeased.\n",
[11787]="70062E81\n1\tDefeat goblins at Haudh Nirui (total: 8)\tGoblins now creep within Haudh Nirui, and Haerandir wants you to defeat as many of the creatures as you can.\n2\tTalk to Haerandir outside Haudh Nirui\tHaerandir is outside Haudh Nirui.\n",
[11788]="7006EC30\n1\tSteal torches (total: 7)\030Spill hog's blood (total: 3)\030Defeat Ekhamâti dôla in their chambers (total: 3)\tYour mission is to infiltrate the Ekhamâti camp, steal their torches, spill hog's blood, and eliminate their dôla all to spread the fear of the Blood Spectre.\n2\tEscape the camp before reinforcements arrive\tEscape the camp before reinforcements arrive and discover you! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[11789]="700084CA\n1\tFind a clue to the Silk-lady's presence in Bail Boglakh\tLornë has asked you to gather some allies and seek out any clues as to the whereabouts of the so-called 'Silk-lady' of Bail Boglakh, an Angmarim fortress to the north of Malenhad.\n2\tBring the tokens to Lornë at Tyrn Lhuig\030Collect Token of the Silk-lady (total: 4)\t\n",
[11790]="7002FD7A\n1\tDefeat a goat, scent a fishing hole, and catch a blood-fish\tGoats and blood-fish can be found among the willows lining the Entwash south-west of Walstow. Héalac asked to catch a blood-fish from the Entwash. In order to do so, you must first scent the water with a freshly-defeated goat.\n2\tBring the blood-fish to Héalac\tHéalac is at Snowbourn. Héalac will be pleased to have the blood-fish that you have caught.\n",
[11791]="700084CE\n1\tLook for Muirnë\030Confront the Bail Róva camp commander\tThe Angmarim camp of Bail Róva is North-west of Tyrn Lhuig, guarding the entrance to the Ram Dúath. Lornë has asked you to look for some sign of her sister and if necessary to confront the outpost's commander for news of Muirnë.\n2\tTalk to Lornë\tLornë is at the hunters' camp in Malenhad. Muirnë was not in Bail Rova, but the Angmarim commander mentioned a Silk-lady who may know more. You should return to Lornë and tell her what you have learned.\n",
[11792]="70054654\n1\tDefeat Rûkhor's forces in Kaslokroz (total: 10)\tRûkhor's forces are camped in Kaslokroz in Cirith Ungol. You should defeat Rûkhor's uruks and goblins.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas can be found near Kaslokroz, Rûkhor's encampment. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[11793]="70008346\n1\tCollect bloodstone trove\tThe bloodstone trove is in the fortress of Tór Gailvin north-east of Aughaire, probably hidden in an out-of-the-way corner. Latharna has asked you to recover the trove of bloodstones that was stolen by the Trév Duvárdain.\n2\tBring bloodstone trove to Latharna\tLatharna is in the Búth Sánkhas in Aughaire, south-east of the market. You have recovered the bloodstone trove from Tór Gailvin and should bring it now to Latharna.\n",
[11794]="70048C4F\n1\tFind the Agarnaith Ranger camp\tThe Agarnaith Ranger camp can be found in North-eastern Gorgoroth, on the border of Agarnaith and Talath Úrui. You should find the Agarnaith Ranger camp.\n2\tTalk to Faeron\tFaeron can be found at the Agarnaith Ranger camp. You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[11795]="70058520\n1\tUse the Instance Finder to enter \"Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold\"\tDurin has called for your aid in the final battle with Gorgar the Ruthless. Use the Instance Finder to enter \"Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold\" on any difficulty.\n2\tTalk to Durin\tThe final battle for Gundabad is about to begin. You should speak to Durin inside Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold.\n3\tFight towards Gundabad\tLead the charge towards Gundabad!\n4\tTalk to Durin\tThe Orcs' trap has been sprung! You should speak to Durin inside Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold.\n5\tSurvive Gorgar's Arena\tGorgar has sprung a trap and forces you and your dwarf allies to fight in his arena. You should fight in Gorgar's arena and survive!\n6\tTalk to Durin\tThe day is won, but Hrímil Frost-heart has returned and claimed Gundabad! You should talk to Durin.\n",
[11796]="7004AAD0\n1\tThe deep sorrow is causing you to cry\tThe Blood-bathed Watcher can be found at the base of Seregost. The Watcher's deep sorrow is causing you to cry.\n2\tTalk to the Blood-bathed Watcher\tThe Blood-bathed Watcher can be found at the base of Seregost. You should talk to the Blood-bathed Watcher again.\n3\tShow the Blood-bathed Watcher your surprise\tThe Blood-bathed Watcher can be found at the base of Seregost. The realization that this was the daughter of Lhaereth surprises you!\n4\tTalk to the Blood-bathed Watcher\tThe Blood-bathed Watcher can be found at the base of Seregost. You should talk to the Blood-bathed Watcher again.\n",
[11797]="70052430\n1\tTalk to Nethlas at the Festival Grounds\tHaerandel says the herbalists are mistaken about the connexion between the purple Anorloth and the Anarlossë of legend, and wants you to tell them.\n2\tTalk to Haerandel and listen to his tale of 'The Blooms of Anarlossë'\tHaerandel is at the Festival Grounds, ready to describe his experiences to both you and the skeptical herbalists from Gondor.\n3\tTalk to Haerandel at the Festival Grounds\tHaerandel is at the Festival Grounds, having told you his memories of the legendary blooms of Anarlossë that once grew where the Men of the West came to settle.\n4\tTalk to Faregild Puddifoot at the Festival Grounds\tFaregild Puddifoot, a hobbit visiting the Festival Grounds, has tried to get your attention.\n5\tTalk to Haerandel\tHaerandel is at the Festival Grounds.\n",
[11798]="70060905\n1\tFind the warg-infested mounds of Glynafon where Hal saw the flower\tThe flower Hal wants grows among the mounds of Glynafon, to the south.\n2\tDefeat wargs around Glynafon (total: 6)\030Collect the rare flower\tWargs can be found prowling around Glynafon. Hal saw the flower he wanted among the old mounds there, but the wargs will make collecting it difficult.\n3\tBring the flower to Hal by the road north of Glynafon\tHal is by the road north of Glynafon, waiting to hear of your success collecting the rare flower.\n",
[11799]="7002BFF9\n1\tBring the strange medallion to one of the Rohirrim border-guard at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tRohirrim may be found at Etheburg in the Brown Lands. You should bring the strange medallion to one of the Rohirrim border-guard.\n",
[11800]="7006228D\n1\tPick up the bread\tDerwen has asked you to bring the bread she baked to her aunt, Henbran. The bread is on the table in Cedrach Amon's house in the Old Forest.\n2\tBring the bread to Henbran\tYou should bring the fresh bread to Henbran and let her know who the blue-cloaked stranger was. Henbran is in the Old Forest.\n",
[11801]="700544A2\n1\tInteract with Bound Spirit\tThe Song-house of Lindalírë can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should free the bound spirits held within the theatre.\n2\tTalk to Dolenthol near the Song-house of Lindalírë\tDolenthol can be found near the Song-house of Lindalírë. You should talk to Dolenthol.\n",
[11802]="7004D06E\n1\tFind and defeat those who lead the thieves (total: 6)\030Recover stolen supplies (total: 8)\030Untie rafts (total: 2)\tYou should defeat enemies, recover the stolen supplies, and untie rafts in the ruins of Esgaroth.\n2\tTalk to Thorlind\tYou should talk to Thorlind, who can be found just outside of Esgaroth-of-old.\n",
[11803]="7005D6F1\n1\tCollect a sack\tDurshulot Book-nabbers can be found in Deepscrave. Some of the goblins of Deepscrave seem to be carrying lumpy sacks. You should investigate their contents.\n2\tCollect sack of books (quantity: see journal)\tDurshulot Book-nabbers can be found in Deepscrave. Some of the goblins of Deepscrave seem to be carrying lumpy sacks. You should investigate their contents.\n3\tBring the sack to Lore-master Rúni in Aslíf, Deepscrave\tLore-master Rúni can be found at Aslíf in Deepscrave. You found a sack of books on one of the goblins in Deepscrave, one of which is an Angmarim book about dragons. Bring the sack of books to Lore-master Rúni.\n",
[11804]="7000C71E\n1\tUse Book-shelf\tThe Book of Festival-law is in the library of the Great Smials in Tuckborough, far to the east of Michel Delving. Will Whitfoot sent you to the Great Smials in Tuckborough to search for the Book of Festival-law.\n2\tTalk to Mayor Will Whitfoot\030Collect Book of Festival-law\tWill Whitfoot is at the Town Hole in Michel Delving, far to the west of Tuckborough. You should return to Will Whitfoot with the Book of Festival-law.\n",
[11805]="70072ECC\n1\tUse 'Aradûni Battle-horn' on allied soldiers in Emax Dûl (total: 8)\tAllied soldiers are still fighting at the four footholds of control in the city. You should find and use 'Aradûni Battle-horn' on allied soldiers in Emax Dûl to lift their spirits.\n2\tTalk to Hanâbu\tYou have rallied the soldiers still fighting in Emax Dûl. You should return to Hanâbu in Nashûbu.\n",
[11806]="7006C6E9\n1\tCollect wild food near Wrackwade in Ambarûl ([see journal]/12)\tRaphûz wants to prove that he can live off the land as the Shagâni do. He asks that you head into the wilds and collect nuts, berries, and meat from across Ambarûl to use on his upcoming journey.\n2\tDeliver the food to Raphûz at Wrackwade\tYou collected food from around Ambarûl. You should deliver what you found and collected to Raphûz at Wrackwade.\n",
[11807]="70009A13\n1\tRead the poster near Basil Gummidge\tThere is a poster on the wall by the stairs near Basil Gummidge in Ost Forod. Basil Gummidge has directed your attention to a poster on the wall near him, asking you to read it, then bring it to him.\n2\tBring wanted poster to Basil Gummidge\tBasil Gummidge is in Ost Forod. You have found a wanted poster placing a bounty on your head at the behest of one Cuthbert Sprunt.\n3\tTalk to Basil Gummidge and travel to the Sparring Circle\tBasil Gummidge is in Ost Forod. Basil Gummidge, the arbiter of Ost Forod, has agreed to ensure that Cuthbert Sprunt does not cheat when you challenge him to single combat. Basil is waiting to speak with you so you can travel together to the Sparring Circle.\n4\tTalk to Basil Gummidge\tBasil Gummidge is in Ost Forod. You have defeated Cuthbert Sprunt, despite his underhanded attempts to cheat at the competition, and should now speak with Basil Gummidge about the victory.\n",
[11808]="70061776\n1\tFind some sign of the goblins' leader at Lhúngobel\tLhúngobel can be found along the River Lune in the north-western reaches of Yondershire. Athal has asked you to travel to Lhúngobel to confront and defeat whichever goblin is now leading them. You should search for some sign of the goblins' leader at Lhúngobel.\n2\tExamine the banner of Angmar\tA banner of Angmar can be found in the ruins of Lhúngobel in the north-western reaches of Yondershire. You have discovered a crude banner of Angmar among the goblins at Lhúngobel. You should examine the banner and continue your search for the goblins' leader at Lhúngobel.\n3\tTalk to Athal\tAthal can be found on a hill just off the road near the border of Ered Luin in Yondershire. You have defeated the goblins' leader, Faltúrz, but a plot between Angmar and the Dourhands loyal to Skorgrím has been revealed. You should talk to Athal.\n",
})
